      "items": [
        {
          "title": "Patchwork: Syncing on AI Standards",
          "link": "https://luma.com/rutu7j4a?tk=l2OxLn",
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0 0 16px 0; padding: 0;    ; font-family: IBM Plex Sans, sans-serif !important; font-size: 19px !important; line-height: 1.2 !important; color: #111111 !important; text-align: left !important\">Everyone's shipping. But are we syncing?<br/> ​Across AI, builders are creating new standards for agents, identity, and payments — sometimes solving problems no one else has seen yet, and other times solving the same ones differently.<br/> ​This is a community breather — a space to step back, compare notes, and align the patchwork of standards.</p>",
          "image": "https://images.lumacdn.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=cover,dpr=2,background=white,quality=75,width=400,height=400/event-covers/g2/472df3f2-f587-456a-8f0f-50956b7038db.jpg",
          "readMoreText": "Read more →"
        }
      ],
      "containerStyles": {
        "backgroundColor": null,
        "padding": "15px 20px",
        "borderRadius": "0px"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "indie-mag-single-column",
      "title": "Lending Library",
      "items": [
        {
          "title": "Friday Gallery - Mother Tongue",
          "link": "https://www.thefridaygallery.com/",
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0 0 16px 0; padding: 0;    ; font-family: Domine, serif !important; font-size: 19px !important; line-height: 1.2 !important; color: #111111 !important; text-align: left !important\">Mitch Jafery's Friday Gallery at The Row DTLA installs the *Mother Tongue* lending library and popup bookstore, a weaving together of perspectives on power and language: from the conversations of plants, to the secret lexicon of an extinct female-only language. It will span cultures, eras, and genres: from protest poetry to con artists, from political philosophy to comic books.</p>",
          "image": "https://imagedelivery.net/gaLGizR3kCgx5yRLtiRIOw/d7dab2cc-e0ac-416c-ccba-c19221d2bd00/w=900",
          "readMoreText": "Go Visit →"
        }
      ],
      "containerStyles": {
        "backgroundColor": null,
        "padding": "15px 20px",
        "borderRadius": "0px"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "books-accessories",
      "title": "Social Climbers",
      "byline": "Shawn Chiki",
      "bylineLink": "https://shawnchiki.xyz",
      "items": [
        {
          "title": "The Night Climbers of Cambridge",
          "link": "https://a.co/d/3uAhuCT",
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0 0 16px 0; padding: 0;    ; font-family: IBM Plex Sans, sans-serif !important; font-size: 19px !important; line-height: 1.2 !important; color: #111111 !important; text-align: left !important\">Parkour in the 1930s?<br/> This pseudonymously authored book (“Whipplesnaith”) describes this secret group, led by the mysterious ‘Butterfly Catcher’, as they scale the Cambridge University buildings in the darkest hours.<br/> (I'm still not sure if this is an elaborate fiction or historically accurate!)<br/> (p.s. Check out Shawn's portfolio to see how this is the perfect background material for his thesis work.)</p>",
          "image": "https://imagedelivery.net/gaLGizR3kCgx5yRLtiRIOw/bfc48b1f-e32c-4b2c-9974-23b2fcb0d500/w=900"
        }
      ],
