    {
      "type": "food-for-thought",
      "title": "From the Discord",
      "items": [
        {
          "title": "Take This Job",
          "category": "We Never Wanted To Make Them Anyway",
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0 0 16px 0; padding: 0;    ; font-family: IBM Plex Sans, sans-serif !important; font-size: 19px !important; line-height: 1.2 !important; color: #111111 !important; text-align: left !important\">I worked at a branding agency in NYC once. Not for very long. Culture clash. I'll never forget the one guy who sat over there with a few contrivances to bind and cobble presentation and PowerPoint pitch decks for 'leave behinds'. No one else could mess with his kit. He'd totally mad dog any one who came around. He was king of his somewhat sad little castle.<br/> Presentation startup Gamma just raised $68 million at a $2.1 billion valuation, boasting 70 million users, profitability, and a lean 52-person team. The company is taking on PowerPoint and Google Slides with AI-powered, instant presentations. Gamma is shaking up the presentation world, turning text into slick slides with AI and racking up millions of users—all while staying lean, profitable, and ambitious enough to take on the industry’s biggest names.</p>",
          "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/11/10/business/dealbook/gamma-ai-fundraise.html",
          "sharedBy": "mtait",
          "channel": "ai-for-powerpoint?",
          "readMoreLink": "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/11/10/business/dealbook/gamma-ai-fundraise.html",
          "readMoreTxt": "Read On →"
        },
        {
          "title": "$300 billion to save the world",
          "category": "Stay On The Rails",
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0 0 16px 0; padding: 0;    ; font-family: IBM Plex Sans, sans-serif !important; font-size: 19px !important; line-height: 1.2 !important; color: #111111 !important; text-align: left !important\">AI is hurtling forward, but the money to keep it from going off the rails is barely a blip. Stanford’s Charles Jones says we should be spending billions more to keep humanity safe—because the stakes couldn’t be higher.</p>",
          "link": "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/11/15/business/dealbook/charles-jones-ai-apocalypse.htm",
          "sharedBy": "ian",
          "channel": "ai-apocolypse",
          "readMoreLink": "https://www.nytimes.com/2025/11/15/business/dealbook/charles-jones-ai-apocalypse.html",
          "paywall": true,
          "readMoreTxt": "Read On →"
        },
        {
          "title": "Windstar Enterprises",
          "category": "Read",
          "description": "<p style=\"margin: 0 0 16px 0; padding: 0;    ; font-family: IBM Plex Sans, sans-serif !important; font-size: 19px !important; line-height: 1.2 !important; color: #111111 !important; text-align: left !important\">Windstar blends psychology and sound to help you rewrite your mental script. Their Solutions Seminar uses music, guided audio, and a unique video brochure to help you break free from old patterns and unlock your potential.Change your story, change your life—Windstar’s Solutions Seminar mixes music, memory, and a dash of 80s flair to help you take charge of your future.</p>",
          "link": "https://www.windstarsolutions.com",
          "image": "",
          "sharedBy": "Solutions",
          "channel": "eh-what",
          "readMoreLink": "https://www.windstarsolutions.com",
          "readMoreTxt": "Read On →"
        }
      ],
